WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:06.022
ai-running-coach: your trail training staff, right inside your editor.

2
00:00:06.872 --> 00:00:13.218
Your watch measures everything: sleep, heart rate variability, pace, elevation.

3
00:00:13.318 --> 00:00:15.440
But who connects the dots?

4
00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:24.412
The coach reads your Garmin data, or Intervals.icu, and writes everything as Markdown, inside your IDE.

5
00:00:25.262 --> 00:00:31.488
Four specialists work together: coach, race strategist, sports doctor and nutritionist.

6
00:00:31.588 --> 00:00:33.710
Keep only the ones you need.

7
00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:42.178
Every morning, three signals decide the session. Today they're in the red: threshold becomes an easy run.

8
00:00:42.278 --> 00:00:45.720
And /why gives the reason, never made up.

9
00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:50.444
The week's plan goes through seven computed guardrails.

10
00:00:50.544 --> 00:00:56.122
Two hard days in a row? Hills move to Thursday, then everything goes to your watch.

11
00:00:56.972 --> 00:01:05.838
On race day, your course is split segment by segment: paces from your own model, three scenarios, and the fuelling to match.

12
00:01:06.688 --> 00:01:09.290
Everything stays yours, in Markdown.

13
00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:16.096
A disposable SQLite index feeds a local dashboard: fitness, fatigue, form.

14
00:01:16.946 --> 00:01:24.828
And the coach follows you everywhere: automatic sync, a push notification, and short commands that get straight to the point.

15
00:01:25.678 --> 00:01:30.872
One clone, one install, a short interview with /coach-setup…

16
00:01:30.972 --> 00:01:33.094
Ready to run smarter?
